   797	
   798	```python
   799	"""Standalone resolution of the Hermes interpreter, source root, and planner
   800	home, plus a boot smoke-check. Deliberately independent of planner.core.config
   801	(this wave is additive; wiring into the core Config is a later wave).
   802	Nothing calls boot_smoke_check this wave; it is unit-tested via the fake
   803	spawn hook only — never with a real child inside pytest."""
   804	
   805	from __future__ import annotations
   806	
   807	import os
   808	from collections.abc import Mapping
   809	from pathlib import Path
   810	from typing import Final
   811	
   812	from planner.minds.gateway import READY_TIMEOUT_DEFAULT, GatewayChild, SpawnFn, spawn_popen
   813	
   814	DEFAULT_HERMES_PYTHON: Final = "~/.hermes/hermes-agent/venv/bin/python"
   815	DEFAULT_PLANNER_HOME: Final = "data/hermes-home"
   816	
   817	ENV_HERMES_PYTHON: Final = "PLAN_HERMES_PYTHON"
   818	ENV_PLANNER_HOME: Final = "PLAN_HERMES_HOME"
   819	
   820	

 succeeded in 0ms:
   821	def resolve_hermes_python(
   822	    value: str | None = None, env: Mapping[str, str] | None = None
   823	) -> Path: ...
   824	
   825	def hermes_src_root(hermes_python: Path | str) -> Path: ...
   826	
   827	def resolve_planner_home(
   828	    value: str | None = None, env: Mapping[str, str] | None = None
   829	) -> Path: ...
   830	
   831	def boot_smoke_check(
   832	    hermes_python: Path | None = None,
   833	    *,
   834	    spawn: SpawnFn = spawn_popen,
   835	    ready_timeout: float = READY_TIMEOUT_DEFAULT,
   836	    env: Mapping[str, str] | None = None,
   837	) -> None: ...
   838	```
   839	
   840	Behaviors:
   841	- `resolve_hermes_python`: precedence explicit `value` → `env[ENV_HERMES_PYTHON]` → default;
   842	  `env` defaults to `os.environ`; the winner gets `Path(...).expanduser()`. (Env override matches
   843	  the house `PLAN_*` config style — core/config.py:93-101; standalone here because W1 must not
   844	  touch existing files.)
   845	- `hermes_src_root(p)`: `~/.hermes/hermes-agent/venv/bin/python` → `~/.hermes/hermes-agent` —
   846	  `Path(p).expanduser()`, then `parents[2]`; if the path is too shallow for `parents[2]`
   847	  (`IndexError`), fall back to `.parent` (documented: assumes the standard venv layout, and the
   848	  guard only feeds the `HERMES_PYTHON_SRC_ROOT` sys.path hint — entry.py:4-12 — so a weird path
   849	  degrades gracefully; `tui_gateway` is importable from the venv python regardless, spike §1).
   850	- `resolve_planner_home`: same precedence with `ENV_PLANNER_HOME` and `DEFAULT_PLANNER_HOME`
   851	  (`data/hermes-home` — provisional, sits in the gitignored data dir; the dedicated-home
   852	  provisioning ticket is spike §5 sub-Q1 and owns the real answer).
   853	- `boot_smoke_check`: spawn → `gateway.ready` → clean exit; raises `GatewayError` on any failure,
   854	  returns `None` on success:
   855	  ```
   856	  python = hermes_python if hermes_python is not None else resolve_hermes_python()
   857	  base = dict(env if env is not None else os.environ)
   858	  base["HERMES_PYTHON_SRC_ROOT"] = str(hermes_src_root(python))
   859	  child = GatewayChild(str(python), base, spawn=spawn)
   860	  try:
   861	      child.wait_ready(ready_timeout)
   862	  finally:
   863	      child.shutdown()
   864	  ```
   865	  Decision (per ticket option): it IS unit-tested, via the injection seam only (tests 27-28
   866	  below). The smoke script additionally exercises the real-child path by hand.
