   870	## 8 · File: `src/planner/minds/smoke.py`
   871	
   872	Human-run only (D6). Never imported by `__init__.py`, never collected by pytest
   873	(`testpaths=["tests"]`), never called by `./verify`. mypy-strict clean (it lives under src/).
   874	
   875	```python
   876	"""Real-gateway smoke run — HUMAN-RUN ONLY. Mirrors spike 01 probes 1-3:
   877	spawn -> ready -> session.create -> prompt.submit -> streamed events ->
   878	message.complete; optional resume leg; deletes the session it created
   879	(best effort). Talks to the REAL gateway and the REAL model: costs one
   880	(or two, with --resume) model round trips and briefly creates a session
   881	in the target HERMES_HOME.
   882	
   883	Usage:
   884	  .venv/bin/python -m planner.minds.smoke
   885	      [--role SKILL] [--home DIR] [--prompt TEXT] [--resume]
   886	      [--hermes-python PATH]
   887	"""
   888	```
   889	
   890	- argparse (stdlib), flags exactly as above. Defaults: `--prompt "Reply with exactly: ok"`;
   891	  `--role` absent → `HERMES_TUI_SKILLS` not set; `--home` absent → `HERMES_HOME` not set (the
   892	  active default home, as the spike's probes 1-3 ran); `--hermes-python` absent →
   893	  `resolve_hermes_python()`.
   894	- Decision: the smoke drives `GatewayChild` directly (not `run_step`) — it mirrors the spike
   895	  probes verbatim, and `run_step` unconditionally sets `HERMES_HOME`/`HERMES_TUI_SKILLS`, which
   896	  would break the absent-flag defaults above. `run_step` itself is exhaustively covered by the
   897	  unit suite; what only a human smoke can prove is the real transport. Env assembled by hand:
   898	  `HERMES_PYTHON_SRC_ROOT` always; `HERMES_HOME`/`HERMES_TUI_SKILLS` only when flags given.
   899	  Concretely:
   900	  1. build env; `child = GatewayChild(...)`; `wait_ready()`; print ready latency.
   901	  2. `created = child.request("session.create", {"source": "minds-smoke", "cols": 100})`;
   902	     print live sid + stored key.
   903	  3. `child.request("prompt.submit", {"session_id": live, "text": prompt})`; loop
   904	     `child.next_event(timeout=120.0)` printing one line per event type, streaming
   905	     `message.delta` text; stop on `message.complete` (print text/status/usage) or `error`
   906	     event (print + exit 1) or `None` (child died, exit 1).
   907	  4. `child.request("session.close", {"session_id": live})`, `child.shutdown()`.
   908	  5. `--resume`: fresh `GatewayChild`, `session.resume {"session_id": stored}`, assert
   909	     `message_count >= 2`, print it; close + shutdown. (Spike §1 probe 3.)
   910	  6. cleanup (best effort, spike §1 probes 1/5: close first, then delete works):
   911	     fresh `GatewayChild` → ready → `session.delete {"session_id": stored}` → print
   912	     `{"deleted": ...}` or the 4023/4007 error → shutdown.
   913	- The event loop here uses a generous explicit `next_event` timeout (120s) — this is an
   914	  interactive tool, not the runner; a stuck smoke should end, not hang a terminal forever.
   915	- `main() -> int`, `if __name__ == "__main__": raise SystemExit(main())`. Exit 0 only if the
   916	  round trip completed.
   917	
